/**
 * The chafa narrow symbol tables this port had not yet carried: the ASCII
 * glyph set (U+0020–U+007E), the Latin/Greek set (U+00A1–U+03F6), the
 * misc-narrow set (U+2190–U+25FC) and the "Symbols for Legacy Computing"
 * block entries of chafa's block table (U+1FB3C–U+1FBAE) that are neither
 * the generated sextant range nor the eighth-block tier.
 *
 * Transcribed VERBATIM from /home/sites/chafa @ 413b76e4d (legacy layout):
 * chafa/internal/chafa-symbols-{ascii,latin,block,misc-narrow}.h — each
 * entry is the 8x8 outline (rows joined by '|', 'X' = set) plus chafa's
 * DECLARED ChafaSymbolTag list. chafa's def_to_symbol() ORs the declared
 * tags with get_default_tags_for_char() minus AMBIGUOUS; this table stores
 * the declared half and {@see SymbolMap} derives the rest, so a glyph's
 * effective tags match the C build.
 *
 * Membership rule is chafa's init_symbol_array(): an outline is narrow when
 * it is 8x8 (64 chars); the 16x8 (128-char) outlines belong to the wide
 * symbols2 array (A-09, unported). chafa-symbols-kana.h is 16x8-only, so
 * the kana set contributes NOTHING to the narrow corpus — see the
 * SymbolMap class docblock for the recorded seam.
 */
